## Exact-head execution claim

Working from integration `main` @ `14d333a225d6b606a8693f85246cacadb1c93ce3` on branch `codex/403-token-layer-audit-current-head`.

Owned write slice for this pass:
- `docs/product/ARQ-UI-UX-TOKEN-LAYER-AUDIT.md`
- one narrowly scoped design-system layer-contract static test under `packages/design-system/src/**`

No runtime restyle is claimed. `apps/web/src/App.tsx` is inspection-only while PR #361 remains active. Fresh open-PR inspection shows no active PR claiming `packages/design-system/src/**`.

Current contradictions already found:
- the previous audit's legacy `--arq-z-modal: 400` finding is stale; current `packages/design-system/src/tokens.css` only imports the brand tokens;
- `WorkspaceSheet` still uses raw `zIndex: 5`;
- workspace context menus still use raw `zIndex: 6` despite the canonical popover tier;
- the workspace skip link uses raw `z-index: 20`;
- `App.tsx` still wraps the command palette in a transformed fixed `zIndex: 10` container, creating a stacking-context risk around the modal tiers, but this file will not be changed in this lane;
- reduced-motion coverage exists for modal/skip-link/refraction motion, but the refraction transition references non-canonical fallback token names.

The requested ZEUS compile command cannot be executed through the current connector-only environment, so it will be recorded as `blocked / not run`, not treated as evidence. CI and repository checks will be used for executable evidence where available.

## #403 exact-head layer handoff

Current audited integration base: `main` @ `2d5a2ae73557049e0d5c2af01f6b0147942b1bcd`.

Inputs for #412:
- canonical global order is raised shell `10`, context HUD `90`, modal backdrop `100`, modal surface `110`, popover `120`, toast `200`;
- `WorkspaceSheet` raw `zIndex: 5` is invalid global-layer drift and can be outranked by raised shell/drawers;
- `TabContextMenu` and phone project-bar More menu use raw `zIndex: 6` despite the canonical popover tier and can sit below raised shell;
- skip link raw `z-index: 20` is an accessibility-sensitive migration candidate, not a reason to lower its visibility;
- refraction lens local `z-index: 1` is justified decoration and uses `pointer-events: none`;
- legacy iPad shell raw `zIndex: 1` values remain tied to #396 consumer/legacy status;
- `App.tsx` wraps the command palette in a fixed transformed raw `zIndex: 10` parent. Because transforms create a stacking context, that wrapper can cap the modal's otherwise-canonical 100/110 children. Do not mutate `App.tsx` until #361 releases ownership, then reconcile/remove this wrapper;
- modal infrastructure itself already uses the canonical backdrop/surface tiers and React Aria modal focus/inert behaviour;
- pointer/occlusion verification should exercise overlapping drawer, sheet, menu, HUD, modal and toast states, not isolated screenshots;
- no arbitrary numeric escalation is an acceptable fix.

PR #498 carries the refreshed audit and narrow layer-drift guard. #403 will record final CI/browser evidence separately.

## #403 performance profiling inputs

Exact audited integration base: `main` @ `2d5a2ae73557049e0d5c2af01f6b0147942b1bcd`.

Please include these measured hot-path candidates in #402 evidence where relevant:
- regular material `saturate(165%) blur(28px)`;
- strong material `saturate(165%) blur(34px)`;
- optical material `blur(16px) saturate(1.06)` plus its multi-layer shadow;
- touch-sheet open/close and layered sheet/drawer states;
- repeated compositing when floating surfaces overlap.

Current mitigations are already present: `contain: paint`, accessibility/platform opaque fallbacks, and nested material explicitly disables additional backdrop filter/shadow. #403 intentionally does not remove blur/shadows based on taste. Measure first, then #489 can enforce budgets.

Execution update for #412

Current implementation branch: `codex/412-overlay-zone-contract` from exact `main` `4184551be3e75636d7feea93fda13699b00b4b43`.

The contract is now centralized rather than duplicated:

- `shell-tokens.css` owns the complete named layer order: 10 / 90 / 95 / 98 / 100 / 110 / 120 / 200;
- `--arq-z-workspace-overlay: 95` and `--arq-z-accessibility: 98` are canonical shell tokens and are pinned by `layer-contract.test.ts`;
- workspace CSS consumes those tokens and contains no local numeric definition for them;
- `WorkspaceSheet` consumes workspace-overlay;
- tab and phone More menus consume popover;
- floating workspace panels/tablet drawers consume workspace-overlay;
- skip link consumes accessibility;
- named canvas zones and pointer-transparent hosts are implemented in `CanvasOverlayZone`;
- #361 remains the external owner of `App.tsx`, so the known command-palette stacking-context wrapper remains an explicit exception and is not modified here.

Pre-format implementation evidence already passed the full unit suite. On the later exact head, #412-owned files were confirmed Prettier-clean; repository-wide `format:check` still stops on the same seven unrelated baseline documents. Final exact-head unit, Engineering Gate and Chromium evidence are running after the canonical-token refinement. No CAD hit-testing, persistence or broad visual redesign is in this PR.
